<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan issues tender to buy jet fuel for Jan 21-31.</title>
<headline>Taiwan issues tender to buy jet fuel for Jan 21-31.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy 32,000 tonnes of jet fuel for January 21-31 1997 delivery, cost-and-freight (c-and-f) Kaohsiung, a CPC official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on December 10 and offers are valid until December 12, he said.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought two 32,000-tonne cargoes of jet fuel for second-half December delivery around $241-$242 per tonne, c-and-f Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>CPC also bought two cargoes of jet fuel for end-October and early November arrival around $247 per tonne, c-and-f Kaohsiung. -- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
